# Marketplace purchase flow

When changing how users discover, configure, cart, or pay for marketplace products:

## Read first (this repo)

- **Product detail:** `app/products/[slug]/page.tsx`, `app/products/[slug]/product-detail-client.tsx`
- **Cart:** `app/cart/page.tsx`, `lib/cart-context.tsx`
- **Add to cart:** `components/shared/product-card.tsx`; calculator-driven flow in `components/shared/calc-price.tsx` where it applies
- **Checkout:** `app/checkout/page.tsx` (and `app/checkout/success`, `app/checkout/cancelled` if post-purchase UX changes)
- **Browse:** `app/marketplace/page.tsx` when listing or navigation to products changes

## Practices

- Reuse existing pages, routing, cart logic, and UI patterns; prefer **small, coherent edits** over re-architecture.
- **Do not change business calculator formulas** (pricing, minimum order, transport, validation math, etc.) in `calc-price.tsx` unless the user explicitly asks; wiring and UI may change if behavior stays equivalent.
- Avoid unnecessary **npm** installs; use what the project already depends on.
- **Romanian copy:** keep domain wording natural and consistent with surrounding strings (e.g. labels like “Cos”, “Finalizare comanda”); URLs may stay as today (`/cart`, `/checkout`) unless the user requests slug changes.
- **Calculator-backed products:** prefer the journey **product page → configurare comandă → coșul meu / review** (configure order, then cart or review), aligned with existing routes and components.
- Before **large** edits, briefly list which files you expect to touch and why.

## Phase 2 — Stripe checkout seam (post-Phase-1 hardening)

Stripe integration is NOT wired in Phase 1. This section locks down the shape
the Phase-2 migration and server action will use, so the current UI and RLS
boundaries keep working when payment lands.

### Planned tables (Phase 2 migration)

- `orders`
  - `id uuid pk`, `buyer_id uuid references profiles(id)`, `seller_id uuid references profiles(id)`,
    `currency text`, `subtotal_cents bigint`, `transport_cents bigint`, `vat_cents bigint`,
    `total_cents bigint`, `status text` (`pending|paid|fulfilled|cancelled|refunded`),
    `stripe_session_id text`, `stripe_payment_intent_id text`, `idempotency_key text unique`,
    `notes text`, `billing_json jsonb`, `shipping_json jsonb`,
    `created_at timestamptz`, `updated_at timestamptz`.
- `order_lines`
  - `id bigserial pk`, `order_id uuid references orders(id) on delete cascade`,
    `listing_id int references marketplace_listings(id)`,
    `title text`, `unit text`, `qty numeric`, `unit_price_cents bigint`,
    `line_total_cents bigint`, `snapshot_json jsonb`.
- `payments`
  - `id uuid pk`, `order_id uuid references orders(id)`, `provider text` (`stripe`),
    `provider_event_id text unique`, `amount_cents bigint`, `status text`,
    `raw_json jsonb`, `created_at timestamptz`.

RLS: `orders`/`order_lines` readable to `auth.uid() in (buyer_id, seller_id)` or admin.
`payments` readable to admin and the buyer/seller of the linked order.
All writes go through SECURITY DEFINER functions or server actions; never direct.

### Server action `createCheckout` (to live in `app/checkout/actions.ts`)

1. Read the client-supplied cart items (ids + quantities ONLY).
2. Re-fetch `marketplace_listings` server-side; recompute every line total
   using DB prices (never trust cart prices from the client).
3. Validate: qty within `available_qty`/`min_order_qty`; items still active.
4. Insert an `orders` row with `status='pending'` and a cryptographic
   `idempotency_key` so duplicate form submits cannot double-charge.
5. Call Stripe `checkout.sessions.create` with `client_reference_id = order.id`,
   store `stripe_session_id` on the order, return the session URL.
6. Stripe webhook (Route Handler `app/api/stripe/webhook/route.ts`) verifies
   the signature, looks up the order by `client_reference_id`, and flips
   `status='paid'` idempotently. Update `components/shared/winner-payment-block.tsx`
   `href="#"` to the stored `stripe_session_id` URL at that point.

### UI touchpoints that must stay stable for Phase 2

- `app/cart/page.tsx`, `lib/cart-context.tsx`: keep the cart shape as
  `{ id, qty }` minimally; anything richer is recomputed server-side.
- `components/shared/calc-price.tsx`: continue to be *display* logic;
  authoritative totals come from the `createCheckout` server recompute.
- `components/shared/winner-payment-block.tsx`: Phase-2 wires the real URL.

